        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaret Reddick, David Sylvian\n- Organizations: Bowling for Soup, Japan, Virgin Records\n- Companies: Samadhi Sound\n- Products: Music Man Axis\n- Roles: lead vocalist, rhythm guitarist, primary songwriter, singer-songwriter, musician, podcaster, actor, voice actor\n\nFacts:\n- David Sylvian was born as David Alan Batt on 23 February 1958 and is an English singer-songwriter and musician.\n- In the late 1970s, David Sylvian came to prominence as the lead vocalist and main songwriter of the group Japan.\n- In the late 1990s, David Sylvian founded the independent record label Samadhi Sound after leaving Virgin Records.\n- Jaret Reddick was born on March 6, 1972 and is an American musician, singer, songwriter, composer, podcaster, actor, and voice actor.\n- Jaret Reddick is best known as the lead vocalist, rhythm guitarist, and primary songwriter for the rock band Bowling for Soup.\n- Jaret Reddick plays a Music Man Axis guitar with a Texas flag design.",
